{
  // Byline: Claude Code · Fable 5.1 · 2026-09-06 — probata build crew v2 (option A of
  // probata/docs/pending-review/2026-09-06-crewai-builder-crew-proposal.md).
  // v2 (owner 21:53-22:00): ccc + smart-explore + DuckDB tools, nemotron primary with OpenRouter FREE fallbacks,
  // exhaustive-search mandates with a search ledger per task, and two new stages: code review + gap analysis.
  // Read-only on the repo; output goes to output/work-package.md and is promoted into
  // probata/docs/pending-review/ by a human or Claude Code.
  "name": "probata_build_crew",

  "agents": ["canon_reader", "code_reviewer", "build_planner", "gatekeeper"],

  // Sequential: each task receives every previous output as context
  "tasks": [
    {
      "name": "constraints_task",
      "description": "Build the EXHAUSTIVE constraints brief for this target.\n\nTARGET: {target}\nRepository root (absolute): {repo_root}\n\nMandatory reads (file tool, absolute paths = repository root + relative path):\n1. AGENTS.md at the repository root - whole file (ATOMICITY rules, knowledge-horizon warnings, Commands table, verification topology, owner delivery and result-persistence rules).\n2. {handoff_path} - whole file (every numbered ruling, every UNRESOLVED item, 'Next steps', 'Owner working-style contract').\n3. {plan_path} with start_line=297 line_count=40 (Stage 0) and start_line=400 line_count=60 (Stage 3 and 3.5).\n4. {changemap_path} - whole file; note every entry that touches the target.\n5. docs/NAMING.md if it exists (naming canon).\n\nMandatory searches - record EVERY one in a 'Search ledger' (tool, query, hits, what you took from it):\n(a) Semantic search (ccc) with at least SIX different phrasings covering: decode subtree / SBV absorption; structured ELT activity registration; read_xml template and DuckDB ELT; stage-graph registration rule; atomicity (one unit = one Activity); parser router signature rule.\n(b) DuckDB sweep of every doc: SELECT filename, regexp_extract_all(content, 'D-[0-9]{{3}}') AS decisions FROM read_text('{repo_root}/docs/**/*.md') WHERE content ILIKE '%<keyword>%' - run it for the keywords read_xml, decode, ELT, stagegraph, 'replace directive'. Then, for every D-number surfaced, locate its row with ripgrep in docs/DECISION_LOG.md and read it with the file tool (start_line/line_count around the hit).\n(c) Ripgrep for D-131, D-149, lowcarbdev/sbv, execute_structured_elt, read_xml across docs/ and modules/engine (the tool already excludes vendor).\n\nSchema doctrine you must carry into the brief: there are NO numbered migrations (D-152/D-153) - sql/bootstrap/schema_snapshot_<date>.sql is the database and a schema change is an edit to it in final form plus scripts/rebuild_platform_from_snapshot.sh; any plan proposing sql/NNNN is a defect. Rules: cite every rule as [file: <relative path>(:line)]; quote short rulings verbatim; never paraphrase from memory; write NOT FOUND for anything you looked for and did not find. The brief is judged on completeness: a rule a reviewer can later find with these tools that you did not list is a defect.",
      "expected_output": "Markdown brief with sections: (A) Binding rules - numbered, one sentence each, each ending with [file: path(:line)]; (B) Already ruled - decision ids (D-nnn, ADR-nnnn) with the verbatim ruling text when short and a one-line meaning for the target; (C) Verification commands the package must include, cited; (D) Open items in the handoff/plan/change map that touch the target, cited; (E) Search ledger - every semantic, DuckDB and ripgrep query with hit counts; (F) Coverage gaps - what was searched for and NOT FOUND; (G) Files read.",
      "agent": "canon_reader"
    },
    {
      "name": "code_review_task",
      "description": "Comprehensive code review of everything the target touches, using the constraints brief from the previous task as the rulebook.\n\nTARGET: {target}\nRepository root (absolute): {repo_root}\n\nScope discovery (mandatory, log every query in a 'Search ledger'):\n- smart-explore 'search' under modules/engine for: structured ELT; register activities; stage graph; parser registry select; sbv adapter; raw record envelope; persist raw generation.\n- ccc semantic search for: how the worker registers Temporal activities; how raw records are persisted through RawRecordEnvelope; where custody hashing happens relative to parsing; how the parser registry selects a handler by signature.\n- ccc structural grep (lang go) for activity-registration call shapes and for direct duckdb.query usage; ripgrep for TODO|FIXME|XXX|panic\\(|log\\.Fatal in the scoped packages.\n\nMinimum review set (use smart-explore outline + unfold; read whole files only when short): modules/engine/activities/elt_structured.go, modules/engine/activities/register.go, modules/engine/profferworker/worker.go, modules/engine/stagegraph/stage.go and registry.go, modules/engine/parser/registry.go, modules/engine/postgres/elt_structured_repository.go, modules/engine/adapters/sbv/sbv.go, modules/forks/sbv/pkg/parseonly/parseonly.go, modules/forks/sbv/internal/importer.go, modules/forks/sbv/internal/sms_xml_importer.go, plus every file your searches show as touched.\n\nReview dimensions: correctness; error handling and silent failures (swallowed errors, early returns that drop records, nil-on-error); retry-safety and idempotency of anything invoked as a Temporal Activity; ATOMICITY boundary violations (hashing, chunking or orchestration inside a parser or activity); resource handling and timeouts; concurrency; test coverage (for each exported symbol in the scoped packages: is there a test? prove it with ripgrep on the symbol name in *_test.go); dead code; comments that contradict the code.\n\nEach finding: id (CR-n), severity BLOCKER/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW, file:line, the quoted line, why it matters, concrete fix, confidence (confirmed/suspected). No finding without a file:line.",
      "expected_output": "Markdown: 1 Scope (files reviewed with line counts, files skipped and why); 2 Findings table (id | severity | file:line | one-line summary | confidence); 3 Findings detail (evidence, impact, fix); 4 Test-coverage table (package | exported symbol | tested? | evidence); 5 Search ledger; 6 Not reviewed and why.",
      "agent": "code_reviewer"
    },
    {
      "name": "gap_analysis_task",
      "description": "Gap analysis between the canon and the code for the target, using the constraints brief (task 1) and the code review (task 2).\n\nTARGET: {target}\nRepository root (absolute): {repo_root}\n\nProduce five gap categories, every row with evidence on BOTH sides:\n(A) Ruled but not implemented - every ruling, plan item or change-map entry relevant to the target that has no code; cite the ruling AND the search that proved absence (smart-explore, ccc, ripgrep - log them).\n(B) Implemented but unruled or undocumented - code paths relevant to the target with no ruling or doc; cite the code AND the doc search that found nothing.\n(C) Docs contradict code - cite both sides with file:line.\n(D) Test gaps - from the review's coverage table plus any you find.\n(E) Schema gaps - the database IS {repo_root}/sql/bootstrap/schema_snapshot_<date>.sql (D-152/D-153; there are no migrations): ripgrep that file for raw_xml, read_xml, template, elt and the tables the target touches; state what the target needs that the snapshot does not define, as an edit to the snapshot in its final form (never as a numbered migration).\n\nEach row: gap id (GAP-n), category, evidence (both sides), impact on the target, suggested closing step. Reference code-review findings by id instead of repeating them. Finish with a Search ledger and a NOT FOUND list.",
      "expected_output": "Markdown: 1 Gap table (id | category | one-line | impact); 2 Gap detail (evidence both sides, closing step); 3 Search ledger; 4 NOT FOUND list.",
      "agent": "code_reviewer"
    },
    {
      "name": "plan_task",
      "description": "Write the execution work package for the target, consuming the constraints brief (task 1), the code review (task 2) and the gap analysis (task 3).\n\nTARGET: {target}\nRepository root (absolute): {repo_root}\n\nExploration is mandatory even though earlier tasks explored - verify what you build on (log every query in a Search ledger):\n- list {repo_root}/modules/engine (one level) and read {repo_root}/modules/engine/go.mod; ripgrep it for 'replace' and 'sbv'.\n- smart-explore outline/unfold the symbols each step will change; smart-explore refs for every symbol you rename or move.\n- ccc semantic search for prior art of anything you propose (e.g. an existing DuckDB template pattern, an existing registration helper).\n- Before designing ANY DuckDB SQL (read_xml / webbed, regexp functions, TRY_CAST), search the DuckDB docs tool and cite the doc URL you relied on.\n- list {repo_root}/sql (one level) for the highest migration number; ripgrep sql/ for read_xml, template, elt.\n- If a fixture or export file is referenced and readable, profile it with the DuckDB file tool.\n\nPackage rules: never propose a numbered migration - schema changes are edits to sql/bootstrap/schema_snapshot_<date>.sql in final form plus a rebuild (D-152/D-153); every statement about current state carries [file: path:line]; every step is ONE unit of work that could be its own Temporal Activity (say which and why); no step deletes anything (park or move instead); each step names its verification command from the constraints brief; every step lists the code-review finding ids (CR-n) and gap ids (GAP-n) it closes; if something was NOT FOUND, say so rather than guessing. Do not write code.",
      "expected_output": "Markdown work package: 1 Objective; 2 Current state (bulleted evidence, each [file: path:line]); 3 Ordered steps (title, files to create or modify, 'one Activity?' yes/no with reason, verification command, closes: CR-/GAP- ids); 4 Acceptance criteria (measurable); 5 Risks and unknowns (NOT FOUND items, unverifiable items); 6 Size estimate; 7 Traceability matrix (every CR- and GAP- id -> step or 'deferred: why'); 8 Search ledger.",
      "agent": "build_planner"
    },
    {
      "name": "review_task",
      "description": "Gate the work package (task 4) against the constraints brief (task 1), using the code review (task 2) and gap analysis (task 3).\n\nRepository root (absolute): {repo_root}\n\nStep 1 - verify before judging: choose EIGHT file:line citations spread across the brief, the review, the gap analysis and the package (prefer load-bearing claims); open each with the file tool using start_line/line_count around the cited line, or ripgrep for the quoted identifier, and record VERIFIED, OFF-BY-N (state the real line) or WRONG. Verify only claims of the form [file: path:line]; never search the repository for the documents' own headings or phrases (e.g. 'gap table'). Budget: at most 12 tool calls in total, then write. A WRONG citation on a load-bearing claim is a REVISE on its own.\nStep 2 - for every binding rule in the brief, mark PASS, FAIL or N/A with a one-line reason and the step it applies to. Flag any step that conflates two units of work, deletes or overwrites data, skips the integration or Go verification commands, or re-opens a question the brief lists as already ruled. Check the traceability matrix: every BLOCKER/HIGH finding and every category-A gap must map to a step or an explicit, justified deferral.\nStep 3 - question-gate residue: only items genuinely undecided after reading all four documents (nothing already ruled, nothing that is a mere parameter).\nStep 4 - verdict: PASS or REVISE with the exact fixes.\n\nFinal output = ONLY your review section, starting with the heading '## Gatekeeper review' and containing: citation checks table, rule table, flags, traceability check, question-gate residue, verdict. Do NOT copy the work package, the gap table or the review table into your answer - a script assembles the deliverable from the stored outputs. Do not add facts that are not in the four documents or the files you opened. Keep it under 2,500 words.",
      "expected_output": "A markdown section that starts with '## Gatekeeper review' and contains: citation checks (citation | VERIFIED/OFF-BY-N/WRONG | note), rule table (rule | PASS/FAIL/N/A | step | reason), Flags, Traceability check, Question-gate residue, and one final line 'Verdict: PASS' or 'Verdict: REVISE - <fixes>'. Nothing else.",
      "agent": "gatekeeper",
      "markdown": true,
      "output_file": "output/gatekeeper-review.md"
    }
  ],

  "process": "sequential",
  "verbose": true,

  // default memory LLM + embedder need OPENAI_API_KEY (crewai/memory/unified_memory.py)
  "memory": false,

  // Runtime inputs; change 'target' to point the crew at other work
  "inputs": {
    "repo_root": "E:/AI_Workspace/Projects/the-platform-workspace/probata",
    "target": "Handoff 2026-09-06 'Next steps' item 3: move the SBV decode subtree into modules/engine/decode/ (dropping the go.mod replace directive), register execute_structured_elt_activity on a worker, and write the first read_xml template for smsbackuprestore, compared with the decoder on fields and counts.",
    "handoff_path": "docs/HANDOFF-2026-09-06-ingest-rulings-and-parser-fix.md",
    "plan_path": "docs/planning/2026-09-03-ingest-redesign-plan-and-sequential-guide.md",
    "changemap_path": "docs/planning/2026-09-06-derived-layers-change-map.md"
  }
}
